Thursday, 6 March 1980  --- JLK					-*-TEXT-*-

This is an ECO to fix the timing jumpers on QUAD CHAOS Rev. 2.


Flush incorrect default jumper setting

Delete			Add

B11-4 : B04-13		B04-8 : B11-4
B04-13 : B04-8

Fix toplevel jumper wiring lossage

A11-9 : E08-14		A11-8 : E08-14
A11-8 : A11-9		A11-6 : C01-6
A11-6 : C01-6
A11-11 : A11-6

Fix toplevel jumper lossage

B03-3 : B03-6		B03-3 : B03-7
B03-7 : B03-8		B03-7 : B03-8
B03-6 : B03-7
B03-5 : B03-10

Fix interval timer bug

F14-13 : B16-15		B16-11 : B16-15

Then follow instructions in AI:CHAOS;QUAD SETUP

----------------------------------------------------------------
4MHz ECO

LMTCLK:

Change jumper B3-6 B3-7 to B3-6 B3-5.  This changes the speed of FCLK.
On some boards, the following wiring may be needed to accomplish this:

	Delete					Add
	------					---
	B3-6 B3-7
	A3-8 B3-3
	B3-3 B3-6				B3-3 B3-7
						A3-8 B3-3
						B3-5 B3-6

LMDETC:

Change timing jumpers.  Remove toplevel wrap on B4-6, B4-8, B11-6, A11-6, A11-8
(only necessary on REV.'s 1 & 2) and then ADD:

			B4-6  B4-13		;lengthen GENCLK
			B4-8  B4-11
			B11-6 B11-13
			A11-6 A11-13
			A11-7 A11-8

NOTE: Some boards require removing B4-7 C1-14 before B4-6 B4-7 can be removed.
      In this case, rewire C1-14 B4-6 before doing B4-6 B4-13.

FCLK/2 fix to allow UNIBUS readout at 8 MHz while cable rate is 4 MHz.

	Delete					Add
	------					---
	A6-7 A16-4
	A6-7 D8-6				A6-7  A16-4
	A6-8 D13-3				A8-11 D8-6
	A6-8 E3-12				D13-3 E3-12
						A9-3  E3-12

